There are two main new errors you might see as part of this.
The first is that assigning an out-of-domain literal to an `enum` type will now error as one might expect:```ts
enum SomeEvenDigit {
    Zero = 0,
    Two = 2,
    Four = 4
}

// Now correctly an error
let m: SomeEvenDigit = 1;
```

